      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1900, Orange hosted America’s first automobile factory, where the Grout company built cars in a dedicated plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Fitchburg Railroad once brought passengers through Orange, but today only freight trains pass through the town’s tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Orange’s Millers River, dammed in 1790, sparked early industry and helped shape the town’s mill‑town character by 1840.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The New Home Sewing Machine Company, founded in Orange, produced 1.2 million machines at its peak in 1892, making it the town’s largest industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Orange’s Memorial Park houses the Massachusetts Peace Statue, a bronze monument erected in 1934 to honor World War I veterans.",
